//  PETPORTS -- SOUR PET TREAT
//
//  A flavored Pet Treat. The upcycler produces these when a Venom Sample-class
//  reagent is in its reagent slot; see scripts/lofty_petports/petports_flavors.config
//  for the reagent list and what each one is worth.
//
//  FLAVOR IS THE WHOLE OF THE PREFERENCE SYSTEM. A unit rolls one preferred
//  flavor and refills more of its fuel bar eating that one. Every other
//  flavor, and the unflavored treat, are worth exactly the same to it -- so
//  feeding a unit the wrong flavor is never a mistake, only a missed bonus.
//  That is what keeps reagents optional rather than a chore.
//
//  A SEPARATE ITEM NAME, NOT A PARAMETER ON petports_petfuel. The whole sorting
//  system keys on names, so distinct names mean a player can route spicy into
//  one crate and sweet into another with the filters that already exist. A
//  parameter would have made the census sum every flavor as one item, which is
//  right for thresholds and wrong for storage.
//
//  PRICE ZERO, AND IT IS LOAD-BEARING. The upcycler values its input by price
//  and refuses anything tagged petports_no_upcycling. Both guards are here for
//  the same reason the unflavored treat has them: a treat worth anything is a
//  treat that can be fed back in, and a laundering loop that pays out slowly is
//  harder to notice than one that pays out fast.
//
//  petports_fuel IS WHAT PUTS THIS IN THE PET TREATS GROUP AT ALL. Do not drop
//  it: fuelWork only sends a unit to empty an upcycler's output slot when some
//  deposit beacon accepts what is in it, so an untagged treat fills a machine
//  and stops it.
//
//  FLAVOR IS A TAG, NOT THE ITEM NAME, and that is what makes this expandable.
//  The deposit-beacon subgroup for this flavor matches petports_flavor_sour
//  rather than petports_petfuel_sour, so a rarity tier added later -- an
//  uncommon or rare Sour treat, a mod's own variant -- sorts into the
//  player's Sour crate on the day it exists, with no manifest edit and no
//  reconfiguring of a beacon they already set up.
//
//  THREE TAGS, THREE JOBS, and none of them is decoration:
//      petports_fuel            this is fuel at all
//      petports_flavor_sour   which flavor it is
//      petports_no_upcycling    it can never be fed back into the machine
//
//  PLACEHOLDER ART: the unflavored treat's flat square in this flavor's
//  colour. Obviously unfinished on purpose, so it cannot be mistaken for a
//  design decision. The colours themselves are NOT placeholder -- they are
//  spread across lightness as well as hue so the seven stay distinguishable
//  under red-green colour blindness, where a naive palette collapses spicy into
//  zesty and savory. Keep that spread when the real art lands.

{
	"itemName" : "petports_petfuel_sour",
	"price" : 0,
	"rarity" : "Common",
	"category" : "petports_fuel",
	"inventoryIcon" : "petports_petfuel_sour.png",
	"description" : "Pressed surplus cut with something that was recently venom. The label insists this is deliberate.",
	"shortdescription" : "Sour Pet Treat",
	"itemTags" : [ "petports", "petports_fuel", "petports_flavor_sour", "petports_no_upcycling" ],
	"maxStack" : 1000
}
